This repository is being prepared for possible open-sourcing. The project owner has not yet
selected a license, so until this file is replaced the code is "all rights reserved" and may
not be used, copied, modified, or redistributed.

Before any publication the owner must:

  1. Decide on the license for the ASEMA source code (for example MIT or Apache-2.0).
     A draft MIT text from an earlier session is kept for convenience in
     docs/LICENSE_CANDIDATE_MIT.txt. It is a candidate only and has NOT been adopted.
  2. Replace this file with the chosen license text and set the correct copyright holder.
  3. Confirm that every redistributed third-party component allows redistribution
     (see THIRD_PARTY in docs/OPEN_SOURCE_READINESS.md).

